%linoac_mouse_step_yaw%
%linoac_mouse_step_pitch%
%linoac_tps%
%linoac_version%
%linoac_total_punishments%
%linoac_total_violations%
%linoac_combat_violations%
%linoac_movement_violations%
%linoac_player_violations%
%linoac_client_brand%
[/CODE]
Online player values are immutable snapshots; unobserved measurements say unknown. CPS is an arm-swing average, not physical mouse clicks.

[SIZE=5][B]10. Developer API[/B][/SIZE]
LinoAPI is registered with Bukkit ServicesManager. It exposes immutable profiles, policies and check state, alert/freeze/reset controls, safe setbacks, explicit flags, waves and statistics. Synchronous lifecycle events support observation/cancellation where specified. Bukkit-facing calls require the main thread. See [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/API.md]API contracts and events[/URL] for exact cancellation effects. The namespace intentionally replaces the original API.

[SIZE=5][B]11. Troubleshooting[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Startup fails: verify Java, PacketEvents 2.14.0 and startup errors.
[*]No alerts: check permission, preference, applicability, enabled state, exemptions, buffer and intervals.
[*]A check cannot enable: missing/no-op slots remain disabled; inspect the catalogue.
[*]No automatic action: check both opt-ins, threshold, delay, cancellation and wave routing.
[*]Connection kick: inspect acknowledgements, latency, pending limits and flood settings.
[*]Reload rejected: fix reported YAML/range errors; existing settings remain active.
[*]Unexpected detection: retain exact ID, server/client versions, ping, environment and audit details; disable the affected rule while investigating.
[*]Compatibility: consult the validation matrix. Other forks, translators, custom physics and multiplayer accuracy need their own evidence.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC]Source[/URL] • [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/releases]Releases[/URL] • [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/issues]Issues[/URL][/CENTER]


[SIZE=5][B]12. Movement, local actions and logs in 0.6.0[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Raw flying ground/air runs include rotation-only packets. JOINED and material clocks retain their separate position cadence.
[*]Raw VEHICLE_MOVE advances mounted state. Positional Bukkit PlayerMoveEvent reads it; NoSaddle evaluates only that Bukkit callback. Rotation-only Bukkit events do not evaluate mounted movement.
[*]Physical Bukkit gliding, cached ELYTRA equipment and acknowledged metadata/action gliding are separate facts. Sulfur uses the acknowledged client block mirror.
[*]Set checks.boatfly-a.dismount, checks.boatfly-b.dismount, checks.entityflight-a.dismount, checks.entityspeed-a.dismount or checks.nosaddle-a.dismount to true for that check's optional local action. Defaults are false. It requires an accepted violation and the same player session and mount; reset, logout and accepted reload cancel pending tasks.
[*]checks.airplace-a.cancel defaults false. checks.hitbox-b.maximum-angle defaults 45 degrees. Per-check speed min-difference fields and movement-exemptions control the documented margins and exclusions.
[*]Log commands show actual page totals, newest matching retained records and distinct read-failure/unavailable messages. Formats, retention and file quotas remain configurable; the first record also respects the quota.
[/LIST]

All nonempty registered source paths now have independent evaluators. The 203-entry catalogue includes four empty callbacks and 24 missing upstream implementations, kept disabled. NoSlow A remains inactive on supported modern servers. Hitbox B, NoSlow B and Jesus D contain documented functional repairs. Read the [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/FIDELITY.md]fidelity ledger[/URL] and [URL=https://github.com/lino9999/LinoAC/blob/main/docs/VALIDATION.md]exact validation report[/URL] for applicability, evidence and limits.
